+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] Burn Recycle (burn_recycle, mp8game=17) 8-player support — ① adaptation (2026-08-17)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# ⚠️ HANDOFF originally said it "might not need a single line changed and naturally supports any player count". **That was wrong.**
+# Only half of it was right. `end_score_labels` always takes `[0]`, so that part really doesn't go out of bounds.
+#
+# ### Structure of this minigame (measured by probe56/57/58 from the stock PCK, not guessed)
+#
+# **A four-station turntable. There isn't a single spawn point coordinate** (`./player spawn parent` has 0 children).
+# Stations are laid out by the **rotation** in `setup_rpc(Vector3(0, 90*counter, 0))`, and the player scene carries its own
+# control panel/levers/piston/score screen/camera and rotates them into place around the world origin. So when counter reaches 4 it's
+# 360°≡0° → **players 5~8 land exactly on top of players 1~4**.
+#
+# Station hardware lives in two places.
+#   * **Inside the player scene** (91 nodes) — control panel, two levers, piston, score screen, camera, 18 item slots
+#     → comes with the player instance, independent of player count, **nothing to do**
+#   * **Main scene, three sets of 4 each** — `belts` / `presses` / `indicators`
+#     → must be duplicated to 8 at runtime, or else
+#       - `belts[seat]` out of bounds → null → `move_items_visual()` errors once per step
+#       - `presses` can't match by `press_id` → `active_press` is always null →
+#         the first statement of `set_eliminated_rpc()` errors and **aborts the whole function** →
+#         `is_dead=true` / `active=false` never run → **an eliminated player can keep playing** (fatal)
+#       - `indicators` can't match → the neighbor's results indicator doesn't light up (cosmetic)
+#
+# ### Why the layout needs no guessing (constitution hard rule #1 — layout belongs to the user)
+#
+# All three prop sets are placed by **pure rotation around the world Y axis**, with these formulas worked back from measurements.
+#   Press       world yaw = 90*press_id + 90        (id0→90° id1→180° id2→270° id3→0°)
+#   Indicator   world yaw = 90*indicator_id - 90    (id2→90° id3→180° id0→270° id1→0°)
+#   Player      world yaw = 90*seat
+# All three are linear functions with "slope = angle step", so going 4→8 just swaps 90 for 45.
+# So duplicating = rotating the original's global_transform 45° around Y, **with no degrees of freedom left to guess**.
+#
+# Numbering rule (derivation in _mp8_expand_stations) — original id i → **2i**, the 45° copy → **2i+1**.
+# This holds whatever the constant term C above is, so C doesn't need to be known.
+#
+# ### Two decisions the user made on 2026-08-17
+#
+#   1. **Eight stations at 45°.** Geometry facts — station radius is 5.2 m, and the adjacent chord drops from 9.95 m at 90° to
+#      5.38 m at 45°. The control panel is 4.66 m wide tangentially → **the control panel itself fits** (0.72 m to spare).
+#      Only the 16.89 m conveyor belt doesn't fit. At 45°, adjacent belts cross at ±2.15 m tangentially.
+#      ⚠️ The first build was packaged with "overlap allowed", and **the user rejected it after seeing screenshots** ("the overlap doesn't look great"),
+#      so it was changed to the **two-tier layout** of MP8_RING_PUSH below. The overlap-allowed approach is obsolete.
+#   2. **Conveyor belt slots cut from 18 to 8~10** (this file uses 9, change MP8_SLOT_COUNT or pass
+#      `mp8burnslots=<N>`). Of the 18 item slots **only 0~3 matter for gameplay**
+#      (0~2 are preview, 3 is the action slot), and the 14 slots 4~17 are purely a visual tail where "unsorted junk rides off".
+#
+# ### ⚠️ Slot count must be server-authoritative (don't change it back to each side computing its own)
+#
+# The slot count sets the length of the `items` dictionary, and the `erase_item_rpc` index is derived from that length
+# (`if i + 1 >= items.keys().size()` in `move_items_data()`). If the two sides have different lengths
+# they each erase different slots → items get scrambled. That's why it's fine if only the host passes `mp8burnslots=`.
+# `_mp8_sync_rpc` broadcasts it to everyone, and the player side takes it from the third parameter of `setup_rpc`.
+#
+# ### ≤4 players, not a single value changes
+#
+# In `_mp8_init()`, ≤4 players takes the vanilla path — 90° angle step, 18 slots, none of the three prop sets duplicated.
+# So 4-player matches are identical to the retail version value for value (including the vanilla misalignment bug below).
+#
+# ### ~~Vanilla belts misalignment bug~~ — **doesn't exist, I miscalculated** (corrected 2026-08-17)
+#
+# The first version asserted "`belts[seat]` picks the neighbor's belt" and even put that in the report to the user.
+# **That was a fake bug derived from the wrong coordinate frame**. Using probe57's frame I concluded station 0 stands at main_003,
+# but at runtime station 0 stands at **main_002** — which is exactly `belts[0]`. **Vanilla was right all along.**
+# The current rebuild logic (array index == station number, determined by geometric anchors) **gives the same result** as the vanilla order.
+# It stays because 8 players need 8 belts, and the order has to come from geometry, not scene order.
+# It's still true that the four belts each have their own material (measured by probe58), so copies need a material of their own.
+#
+# ### Not done yet (② scoring, bound by the "scoring hard rule", waiting for separate confirmation from the user)
+#
+#   * In `check_game_end()` the survivor gets `player_count` (= 8 in an 8-player match) while the last to die gets 6
+#     → **a 2-point jump between 1st and 2nd**, every other step is 1. Exactly the same shape as Junk Platform T13,
+#     with the same fix (`dead_players.size()`), **but that's phase ②, not touched this round.**
+#     Also, disconnected players don't enter `dead_players` (`player_disconnected` only erases),
+#     so `player_count` is inflated too — fix both at the same spot in one go, not in two passes.
+#   * **Pacing** — one player is eliminated per round, so 8 players = 7 rounds before a result (4 players is 3), roughly doubling the match length.
+#     Whether to eliminate two per round is a design decision waiting on the user.
+#   * This round added `_mp8_log_scores()`, which only logs and **changes no scores**, for cross-checking in phase ②.
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
